{#
mail/_jobs_indicator.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Background work, in the topbar, and only when there is any.

A whole-view action — "mark all 5,455 read" — runs on a worker now, so the page
answers immediately and the work happens somewhere the user cannot see. This is
where they can see it.

NOT RENDERED WHEN THERE IS NOTHING TO SAY, and that is the whole design of it.
An indicator that is always present is another permanent fixture to learn to
ignore; one that appears only while something is happening is read the moment it
appears. The frame collapses to nothing when the list is empty.

A job that SUCCEEDED does not linger — see BackgroundJobRepository::findVisibleForUser.
It has already changed the list the user is looking at, so an indicator
reporting it says something they can see, and an indicator that appears and
disappears on its own is a topbar that reflows for no reason. A FAILURE is the
opposite: nothing changed, and if this does not say so, nothing does.

Refreshed by core--mercure on `jobs.changed`, which carries no state: the row is
the record and a missed nudge costs one stale render, never a wrong answer.
#}
{# NO `src`, deliberately. A frame with one fetches itself on every page load,
   which is a request per page for every user answering "nothing is happening"
   almost every time — and it broke the appearance preview's assertion that it
   loads no mail, which was right to complain.

   The topbar renders this with whatever jobs exist, which is one indexed query
   it is already making a page render for. From then on it is replaced: by the
   response to starting a job, and by mail--jobs when Mercure says one moved.
   The route stays, because that is what mail--jobs re-reads. #}
{# An import is shown here too, and is not a job: `imports` is a list of
   App\Domain\DTO\Mail\ImportLine, one per account still bringing in its
   history, worked out from the account each time (see ImportProgress). It
   counts as something running, so the button is there and moving for as long
   as mail is still arriving from the past. #}
{% set jobs = jobs|default([]) %}
{% set imports = imports|default([]) %}
{# `contents`, so an empty frame is no box at all: as a flex item it would
   still claim a gap beside the search box and push it off centre. #}
<turbo-frame id="jobs-indicator" class="contents">
    {% if jobs|length > 0 or imports|length > 0 %}
        {% set active = jobs|filter(j => j.isActive())|length + imports|filter(i => false == i.waiting)|length %}
        {% set failed = jobs|filter(j => j.state.value == 'failed')|length %}

        {# From xl up it hangs off the left edge of the search group instead
           of sitting in it, so the search box stays in the middle of the
           topbar whether or not anything is running. Narrower than that there
           is no room to its left and it takes a place in the row as an icon. #}
        <div class="relative xl:absolute xl:right-full xl:top-1/2 xl:-translate-y-1/2 xl:mr-2" data-controller="ui--dropdown">
            {# A tinted chip with words on it, not a bare icon. It used to be
               a muted glyph that faded in and out — from barely visible to
               nearly invisible — beside five other muted glyphs. Tinted rather
               than filled: a solid block of accent beside the search box
               outshouted Compose, and this is a notice, not an action. The
               colour says which of three things is true: running (accent),
               failed (danger), or stopped with something to read (plain).

               The label goes below xl, where the chip is in the row and has
               no room for it; the chip and its colour stay. #}
            {% set importing = imports|filter(i => false == i.waiting)|first %}
            {% if failed > 0 %}
                {% set tone  = 'border border-danger/40 bg-danger/10 text-danger hover:bg-danger/15' %}
                {% set label = 'jobs.button.failed'|trans %}
            {% elseif active > 0 %}
                {% set tone  = 'border border-accent/40 bg-accent-soft text-accent hover:bg-accent/20' %}
                {% set label = importing
                    ? (importing.total is not null
                        ? 'jobs.button.importing_percent'|trans({ '%percent%': importing.percent() })
                        : 'jobs.button.importing'|trans)
                    : 'jobs.button.working'|trans %}
            {% else %}
                {% set tone  = 'border border-line text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover' %}
                {% set label = imports|length > 0 ? 'jobs.import.waiting'|trans : 'jobs.heading'|trans %}
            {% endif %}
            <button
                type="button"
                data-action="click->ui--dropdown#toggle"
                data-jobs-button
                class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-center gap-1.5 h-8 px-2.5 max-xl:w-8 max-xl:px-0 rounded-lg
                       text-xs font-medium whitespace-nowrap transition-colors flex-shrink-0 {{ tone }}"
                aria-label="{{ 'jobs.heading'|trans }}"
                title="{{ 'jobs.heading'|trans }}"
            >
                {# Turning only while something is actually running: a still
                   glyph for "here is what happened" and a moving one for
                   "still going" is the difference the eye reads first. #}
                <i class="fa-solid {{ failed > 0 ? 'fa-triangle-exclamation' : (active > 0 ? 'fa-arrows-rotate fa-spin' : 'fa-list-check') }} text-xs"
                   aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <span class="max-xl:hidden">{{ label }}</span>
            </button>

            {# The `hidden` ATTRIBUTE, not the Tailwind class.
               ui--dropdown opens a menu by clearing `hidden` as a property, and
               it never touches classes. With the class instead, the panel was
               display:none no matter what the controller did — and because the
               attribute was absent, the FIRST click read the menu as already
               open and closed it. So the button pulsed away saying work was
               running, and clicking it did nothing at all, for ever. Every
               other dropdown in the app uses the attribute; this was the one
               that did not. #}
            <div
                data-ui--dropdown-target="menu"
                data-enter="slide-down"
                hidden
                class="absolute left-0 max-md:left-auto max-md:right-0 top-full mt-1 z-30 w-80 text-left
                       rounded-pane bg-surface
                       border border-line shadow-pop p-2 text-sm"
            >
                <p class="px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'jobs.heading'|trans }}</p>

                <ul class="mt-1 space-y-1">
                    {# Imports lead: they are the long ones, and the answer to
                       "why is my Inbox still filling up". #}
                    {% for line in imports %}
                        <li class="rounded-lg px-2 py-2 {{ line.waiting ? '' : 'bg-accent-soft/40' }}" data-import-line>
                            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                                <span class="text-xs font-medium text-ink truncate">
                                    {{ 'jobs.import.heading'|trans({ '%account%': line.account.displayAddress }) }}
                                </span>
                                <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint tabular-nums shrink-0">
                                    {% if line.total is not null %}
                                        {{ line.done|number_format }} / {{ line.total|number_format }}
                                    {% else %}
                                        {{ 'jobs.state.queued'|trans }}
                                    {% endif %}
                                </span>
                            </div>

                            {% if line.total is not null %}
                                <div class="mt-1.5 h-1 rounded-full bg-line overflow-hidden">
                                    <div class="h-full bg-accent transition-all duration-300"
                                         style="width: {{ line.percent() }}%"></div>
                                </div>
                            {% endif %}

                            {# What it is on, or that it is not on anything. A
                               bar that has stopped says nothing by itself;
                               "waiting" at least says it is known to have. #}
                            <p class="mt-1 text-[11px] text-ink-faint truncate">
                                {% if line.waiting %}
                                    {{ 'jobs.import.waiting'|trans }}
                                {% elseif line.label %}
                                    {{ 'jobs.import.folder'|trans({ '%folder%': line.label|label_name }) }}
                                {% elseif line.folder %}
                                    {{ 'jobs.import.folder'|trans({ '%folder%': line.folder.label ? line.folder.label|label_name : line.folder.name }) }}
                                {% else %}
                                    {{ 'jobs.import.newest_first'|trans }}
                                {% endif %}
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                    {% for job in jobs %}
                        <li class="rounded-lg px-2 py-2 {{ job.isActive() ? 'bg-accent-soft/40' : '' }}">
                            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                                <span class="text-xs font-medium text-ink truncate">
                                    {{ job.kind.labelKey()|trans }}
                                </span>
                                <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint tabular-nums shrink-0">
                                    {% if job.state.value == 'failed' %}
                                        {{ 'jobs.state.failed'|trans }}
                                    {% elseif job.state.value == 'done' %}
                                        {{ 'jobs.state.done'|trans({ '%count%': job.total }) }}
                                    {% elseif job.total > 0 %}
                                        {{ job.processed }} / {{ job.total }}
                                    {% else %}
                                        {{ 'jobs.state.queued'|trans }}
                                    {% endif %}
                                </span>
                            </div>

                            {% if job.isActive() and job.total > 0 %}
                                {# Width from the job's own percent(), which
                                   floors and never reports more than 100 — a
                                   bar that reaches the end before the work does
                                   is worse than no bar. #}
                                <div class="mt-1.5 h-1 rounded-full bg-line overflow-hidden">
                                    <div class="h-full bg-accent transition-all duration-300"
                                         style="width: {{ job.percent() }}%"></div>
                                </div>
                            {% endif %}

                            {% if job.failureReason %}
                                <p class="mt-1 text-[11px] text-danger break-words">{{ job.failureReason }}</p>
                            {% endif %}
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</turbo-frame>
